# hwdef.dat for the Nano H743 AIO (STM32H743VIT6 FC + integrated 4-in-1 ESC)
# Sreesai Arjun Engineering - Revision 13.0 / 150
#
# Processed by libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/scripts/chibios_hwdef.py.
# Rev 6.0 scope: deterministic DMA allocation for USART1, SPI1, SPI4 and
# SDMMC1 (4-bit microSD) so that no latency-critical peripheral shares a
# DMA stream. See "DMA STREAM BUDGET" below and README.md section
# "Revision 6.0 Engineering Changelog".
# Rev 10.0 scope: bidirectional DShot600 timer-channel / input-capture
# configuration and ESC telemetry processing (see the TIM1 block below and
# "Revision 10.0 Engineering Changelog").
# Rev 11.0 scope: dual-IMU synchronisation. Both ICM-42688-P share one
# 32.768 kHz CLKIN (RTC mode), IMU2 gains its DRDY line, and each IMU has a
# dedicated supply filter (see the IMU block and "Revision 11.0 Engineering
# Changelog").
# Rev 13.0 scope: AT7456E analog OSD on SPI2 (U5, 5 MHz SCLK for timing
# margin), 6-pin SH1.0 digital VTX connector J1 on USART1 (+ UART7_RX for the
# DJI HDL / SBUS pin) and the switchable 9 V / 12 V 2 A VTX BEC (U6
# TPS62933, VTX_PWR / VTX_12V_SEL relays, VTX_VSENSE ADC).  See
# analysis/osd_vtx_bec_analysis.py and "Revision 13.0 Engineering Changelog".

# MCU class and specific type (format: MCU <series> <type>)
MCU STM32H7xx STM32H743xx

# Board ID. PROVISIONAL - 5743 is unallocated in
# Tools/AP_Bootloader/board_types.txt as of this revision; it MUST be
# registered upstream (AP_HW_NANO_H743_AIO) before public release.
APJ_BOARD_ID 5743

# 24 MHz HSE crystal (Rev 7.0: Y1 TXM24M0004322FBCDO00T, CL 12 pF, C1/C2
# 16 pF C0G - see kicad/nano-h743-aio.kicad_sch and
# analysis/hse_vdda_analysis.py).  ArduPilot's stm32h7_mcuconf.h derives the
# PLLs from OSCILLATOR_HZ; raw PLL values are NOT hwdef keywords.
#   PLL1: 24 MHz /M3 = 8 MHz x N120 = 960 MHz VCO, /P2 = 480 MHz SYSCLK
#   PLL3: 24 MHz /M6 = 4 MHz x N72 = 288 MHz VCO, /Q6 = 48 MHz USB (exact)
# Rev 6 used 25 MHz, which cannot run at 480 MHz: stm32h7_mcuconf.h has no
# custom-clockrate PLL set for 25 MHz and stops with
# "#error Unable to configure custom clockrate".
# 480 MHz requires revision V silicon (all current STM32H743VIT6 date codes).
OSCILLATOR_HZ 24000000
MCU_CLOCKRATE_MHZ 480

# 2 MB flash; first 128 kB sector reserved for the bootloader
FLASH_SIZE_KB 2048
FLASH_RESERVE_START_KB 128

# Parameter storage in the last two 128 kB flash sectors (14, 15)
STORAGE_FLASH_PAGE 14
define HAL_STORAGE_SIZE 32768

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USB / debug
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PA11 OTG_FS_DM OTG1
PA12 OTG_FS_DP OTG1
PA8  VBUS INPUT OPENDRAIN

PA13 JTMS-SWDIO SWD
PA14 JTCK-SWCLK SWD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPI1 - IMU1 (primary) ICM-42688-P   [DMA: SPI1_RX + SPI1_TX, NOSHARE]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PA5 SPI1_SCK  SPI1
PA6 SPI1_MISO SPI1
PA7 SPI1_MOSI SPI1
PA4 IMU1_CS   CS
PC4 IMU1_DRDY INPUT

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPI4 - IMU2 (secondary) ICM-42688-P [DMA: SPI4_RX + SPI4_TX, NOSHARE]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PE2 SPI4_SCK  SPI4
PE5 SPI4_MISO SPI4
PE6 SPI4_MOSI SPI4
PE4 IMU2_CS   CS
# Rev 11.0: IMU2 INT1 data-ready. EXTI1 - deliberately a different EXTI line
# from IMU1_DRDY (PC4 = EXTI4) so the two can never share an EXTI vector.
PE1 IMU2_DRDY INPUT

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rev 11.0 - shared IMU sample clock (CLKIN / RTC mode)
#
# Y2 (SX2M32.768KM20F30TNN, 32.768 kHz CMOS, +/-30 ppm) drives pin 9
# (INT2/FSYNC/CLKIN) of BOTH ICM-42688-P through one 33R source resistor per
# branch (R14 -> U2, R15 -> U3).  With RTC_MODE=1 and PIN9_FUNCTION=CLKIN
# each IMU derives its ODR from this clock, so IMU1 and IMU2 sample on the
# same time base: zero relative drift, constant phase offset.
#   ODR scales with f_CLKIN / 32 kHz: nominal 8 kHz -> 8192 Hz.  ArduPilot's
#   _update_sensor_rate() tracks the observed rate (+/-5 % window) so the
#   +2.4 % shift is absorbed by the notch/FFT rate estimate.
# The INVENSENSEV3_CLKIN_BITMASK bit index is the gyro instance (imu1 = 0,
# imu2 = 1).  Upstream only honours it for IIM-42652; patch
# ardupilot/patches/0002-* extends RTC mode to ICM-42688 and adds the
# loss-of-clock fallback to the internal oscillator.
#
# PD12 (TIM4_CH1) monitors the clock through a 1k isolation resistor (R16)
# so a dead oscillator is observable by the MCU (firmware/imu_sync).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PD12 IMU_CLKIN_MON INPUT GPIO(91)
define INVENSENSEV3_CLKIN_BITMASK 3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPI2 - AT7456E analog OSD          [DMA: SPI2_RX + SPI2_TX, shareable]
#
# Rev 13.0: U5 AT7456E (LCSC C82351, HTSSOP-28-EP), all three supplies on the
# filtered +3V3_OSD rail (FB5) so SDOUT swings 0..3.3 V into PB14 and every
# MCU-driven input stays inside its VDVDD+0.3 V abs-max.  33R source
# termination R30..R33 (pin 1 = this hwdef net).  27 MHz crystal Y3.
# /RESET is pulled up only (R29 10k); AP_OSD_MAX7456 probes with a VM0
# software reset.  LOS / HSYNC / VSYNC are unused (driver polls STAT).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PB13 SPI2_SCK  SPI2
PB14 SPI2_MISO SPI2
PB15 SPI2_MOSI SPI2
PB12 OSD1_CS   CS

# SPI devices: name bus devid cs mode low_speed high_speed
# ICM-42688-P is rated to 24 MHz.  ArduPilot picks the first power-of-two
# divisor of (kernel clock / 2) that is <= the requested 16 MHz, so the
# actual SCLK is (Rev 7.0, 24 MHz HSE / 480 MHz; identical to Rev 6 values):
#   SPI1 kernel = PLL1_Q  80 MHz -> 40 -> 20 -> 10.0 MHz SCLK (IMU1)
#   SPI4 kernel = PLL2_Q 100 MHz -> 50 -> 25 -> 12.5 MHz SCLK (IMU2)
# Both are inside the 24 MHz limit; the asymmetry is accepted (FIFO reads at
# 8 kHz need < 2 MHz effective).  A request of 20*MHZ would give 20/25 MHz.
SPIDEV imu1 SPI1 DEVID1 IMU1_CS MODE3  2*MHZ 16*MHZ
SPIDEV imu2 SPI4 DEVID1 IMU2_CS MODE3  2*MHZ 16*MHZ
# Rev 13.0 OSD speed: SPI2 kernel = PLL1_Q 80 MHz (same as SPI1).  10*MHZ
# gave 80/8 = 10.000 MHz = the AT7456E tCP(min) 100 ns limit with ZERO
# margin.  AP_OSD_MAX7456 never calls set_speed(), so the LOW speed value is
# the one used.  8*MHZ -> divisor search 40 -> 20 -> 10 -> 5 => 5.000 MHz
# (tCP 200 ns, 2x margin).  Worst-case 484-byte flush = 0.78 ms per 100 ms.
SPIDEV osd  SPI2 DEVID4 OSD1_CS MODE0  8*MHZ  8*MHZ

IMU Invensensev3 SPI:imu1 ROTATION_NONE
IMU Invensensev3 SPI:imu2 ROTATION_PITCH_180
define HAL_DEFAULT_INS_FAST_SAMPLE 3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# I2C1 - DPS310 baro + external compass (I2C DMA is disabled by default on
# H7 by chibios_hwdef.py, so I2C1 consumes no DMA stream)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PB6 I2C1_SCL I2C1
PB7 I2C1_SDA I2C1
I2C_ORDER I2C1

BARO DPS310 I2C:0:0x76

define ALLOW_ARM_NO_COMPASS
define AP_COMPASS_PROBING_ENABLED 1
define HAL_I2C_INTERNAL_MASK 0
define HAL_COMPASS_AUTO_ROT_DEFAULT 2

# Rev 12 - I2C1 timing (analysis/baro_i2c_analysis.py -> baro_i2c_report.json).
# ArduPilot's HAL_I2C_MAX_CLOCK default is 100000, so without this I2C1 runs
# at 100 kHz (H7_100 TIMINGR) whatever get_device() asks for.
define HAL_I2C_MAX_CLOCK 400000
# I2CCLK = PLL3_R = 32 MHz. Default H7_400 0x00300F38 (SCLH 15, SCLDEL 3):
# tHIGH 500 ns + filter delay is < 600 ns once the SCL-high detection
# threshold sits low in the 0.3..0.7 VDD window, and tSCLDEL 125 ns breaks
# RM0433 tSCLDEL >= tr + tSU;DAT(100 ns) for any tr > 25 ns.
# 0x00D01A2D: PRESC 0, SCLDEL 13 (437.5 ns), SDADEL 0, SCLH 26, SCLL 45.
# Fm-compliant for any tr <= 300 ns (worst tLOW 1447, tHIGH 658 ns),
# 276..396 kHz worst-case, ~355 kHz typical (same period as the default).
# DNF stays 0 / analog filter on: ArduPilot writes CR1 from i2ccfg.cr1
# (SMBHEN only), so neither is settable from hwdef.
define HAL_I2C_H7_400_TIMINGR 0x00D01A2D
# 100 kHz path: I2C1 is the external bus (HAL_I2C_INTERNAL_MASK 0). If any
# driver opens it at 100 kHz (INA2xx/INA3221/SMBus/LTC2946 battery monitors,
# MCP40D1x DAC), the I2CDevice ctor on H7 lowers the WHOLE bus to
# HAL_I2C_F7_100_TIMINGR (not the H7 one). Default 0x30812E3E is an F7
# 54 MHz value: at 32 MHz 62..71 kHz with tSCLDEL 1125 ns < RM0433
# tr(1000) + tSU;DAT(250 ns). 0x4080231E: PRESC 4 (156.25 ns), SCLDEL 8
# (1406 ns), SDADEL 0, SCLH 35, SCLL 30. UM10204 Sm-compliant for any
# tr <= 1000 ns (worst tLOW 4853, tHIGH/tSU;STA 4739, tBUF 4724 ns),
# 78..93 kHz worst-case. H7_100 (only used if MAX_CLOCK <= 100 kHz) is set
# to the same value so both 100 kHz paths are compliant.
define HAL_I2C_F7_100_TIMINGR 0x4080231E
define HAL_I2C_H7_100_TIMINGR 0x4080231E
# Bus clear (kept default HAL_I2C_CLEAR_ON_TIMEOUT 1): at boot and after a
# timeout with SDA low, SCL is toggled push-pull 10 clocks at ~50 kHz.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FDCAN1 - DroneCAN via TCAN334 (FDCAN uses its own message RAM, no DMA)
# TCAN334 STB has an internal pull-up: it must be actively driven LOW or the
# transceiver stays in standby and the bus is dead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PD0 CAN1_RX CAN1
PD1 CAN1_TX CAN1
PD3 GPIO_CAN1_SILENT OUTPUT PUSHPULL SPEED_LOW LOW GPIO(70)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SDMMC1 - microSD, 4-bit bus
# On STM32H7 SDMMC1 uses its internal IDMA master, NOT a DMA1/DMA2 stream,
# so it is deliberately absent from the stream budget. IDMA can only reach
# AXI SRAM / SRAM1-3 (not DTCM); ArduPilot's FATFS layer bounce-buffers
# through DMA-safe memory, so no extra config is needed here.
# PC10/PC11/PC12/PD2 are therefore unavailable for UART4/UART5/SPI3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PC8  SDMMC1_D0  SDMMC1
PC9  SDMMC1_D1  SDMMC1
PC10 SDMMC1_D2  SDMMC1
PC11 SDMMC1_D3  SDMMC1
PC12 SDMMC1_CK  SDMMC1
PD2  SDMMC1_CMD SDMMC1
define HAL_OS_FATFS_IO 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integrated 4-in-1 ESC - bidirectional DShot600 on TIM1 CH1..CH4
# (Rev 10.0 - validated by tools/validate_bdshot.py against ArduPilot source)
#
# Output: one TIM1_UP DMAR burst writes CCR1..CCR4 for all four motors.
#
# eRPM input capture (RCOutput_bdshot.cpp, bdshot_setup_group_ic_DMA):
#   BIDIR on CH1 and CH3 only.  CH2 has no IC DMA of its own, so ArduPilot
#   captures it on IC1 with CC1S=10 (TI2 -> IC1) and borrows CH1's DMA
#   request; CH4 likewise on IC3 (TI4 -> IC3).  That pairing only exists
#   within CH1/CH2 and CH3/CH4, which is why the BIDIR channels are 1 and 3.
#   dma_resolver.py then puts TIM1_CH1 and TIM1_CH3 on the TIM1_UP stream
#   (DMA1-0) and RCOutput re-points the DMAMUX request between UP and CHx for
#   each receive window (has_shared_ic_up_dma()).
#   No complementary (CHxN) outputs: ArduPilot cannot input-capture them.
#
# Round-robin: one pwm_group (TIM1) captures ONE motor per DShot frame
# (bdshot.curr_telem_chan, bdshot_find_next_ic_channel), so each motor's
# eRPM refreshes at f_dshot / 4.  defaults.parm SERVO_DSHOT_RATE 4 gives
# evenly spaced 1600 Hz frames -> 400 Hz per motor at SCHED_LOOP_RATE 400.
#
# Timing at MCU_CLOCKRATE_MHZ 480 (TIM1 on APB2, 240 MHz kernel clock):
#   DShot600 out: PSC 49 -> 4.8 MHz, 8 ticks per 1.667 us bit (exact);
#   frame = 16 + 1 pre + 2 post slots = 19 bits = 31 us (pulse_send_time_us)
#   GCR reply 750 kbit/s, 21 bits = 28.0 us, ~30 us after the frame; the
#   receive window ArduPilot arms is 31 + 30 + 10 = 71 us
#   IC prescaler telempsc = 240e6/750e3/16 - 1 = 19 -> 83.3 ns/tick,
#   exactly 16 ticks per GCR bit (no rounding drift; tolerates +/-14 % ESC
#   clock error, firmware/bdshot_telem test T3).
#   Bidir cycle (frame + receive window) 102 us of the 625 us period (16 %).
#
# Electrical: ArduPilot sets these pins PUSHPULL + PULLUP at OSPEED MID1 in
# bidir mode.  Each line has a 100R 0402 series resistor (R4..R7, schematic
# nets TIM1_CHn -> ESCn_DSHOT) placed within 3 mm of the MCU pin to damp
# edge ringing into the ESC MCU input.  No external pull-up: the ESC
# bootloaders (AM32, BLHeli_32) treat a signal line that is high at power-on
# as a host waiting for 1-wire passthrough and delay the jump to the
# application; the FC pin is high-Z until ArduPilot configures it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PE9  TIM1_CH1 TIM1 PWM(1) GPIO(50) BIDIR
PE11 TIM1_CH2 TIM1 PWM(2) GPIO(51)
PE13 TIM1_CH3 TIM1 PWM(3) GPIO(52) BIDIR
PE14 TIM1_CH4 TIM1 PWM(4) GPIO(53)

# Beeper (timer alarm, no DMA)
PA15 TIM2_CH1 TIM2 GPIO(32) ALARM

# Status LED
PE3 LED0 OUTPUT LOW GPIO(90)
define AP_NOTIFY_GPIO_LED_1_ENABLED 1
define AP_NOTIFY_GPIO_LED_1_PIN 90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Battery sense (ADC1, one DMA stream)
# PC0 = ADC123_INP10, PC1 = ADC123_INP11
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PC0 BATT_VOLTAGE_SENS ADC1 SCALE(1)
PC1 BATT_CURRENT_SENS ADC1 SCALE(1)
define HAL_BATT_MONITOR_DEFAULT 4
define HAL_BATT_VOLT_PIN 10
define HAL_BATT_CURR_PIN 11
define HAL_BATT_VOLT_SCALE 10.9
define HAL_BATT_CURR_SCALE 50.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Serial ports
# SERIAL0 = USB, SERIAL1 = USART1, SERIAL2 = USART2, SERIAL3 = USART3,
# SERIAL4 = UART7 (RX only, VTX connector pin 6, Rev 13.0)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERIAL_ORDER OTG1 USART1 USART2 USART3 UART7

# USART1 - high-rate full-duplex link (DJI O3 / Walksnail MSP DisplayPort,
# or MAVLink2 to a companion at up to 2 Mbaud). Both directions on
# dedicated, non-shared DMA streams.   [DMA: USART1_RX + USART1_TX, NOSHARE]
PA9  USART1_TX USART1
PA10 USART1_RX USART1

# USART2 - RC receiver (CRSF / ELRS @ 420 kbaud). RX on DMA so frames are
# never lost to ISR latency; low-volume telemetry TX is interrupt-driven.
PD5 USART2_TX USART2 NODMA
PD6 USART2_RX USART2

# USART3 - GPS (+ compass on I2C1). RX on DMA; config/RTCM-free TX is
# interrupt-driven.
PD8 USART3_TX USART3 NODMA
PD9 USART3_RX USART3

# Rev 13.0: UART7 RX only (PE7) - pin 6 of the digital VTX connector J1
# (DJI HDL / SBUS from DJI goggles' remote, through R44 1k).  SBUS is 100k
# 8E2 inverted; the H7 USART inverts in hardware (SERIAL4_OPTIONS bit 0).
# NODMA: 100 kbaud is trivially interrupt-driven and the DMA budget below
# stays at 12/16 streams.  PE8 (UART7_TX) remains unassigned.
PE7  UART7_RX UART7 NODMA

define DEFAULT_SERIAL1_PROTOCOL SerialProtocol_MSP_DisplayPort
define DEFAULT_SERIAL2_PROTOCOL SerialProtocol_RCIN
define DEFAULT_SERIAL3_PROTOCOL SerialProtocol_GPS

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rev 13.0 - digital VTX power: 9 V / 12 V 2 A BEC (U6 TPS62933DRLR, 500 kHz)
#
# VTX_PWR  (PD10) -> R39 1k -> U6 EN.  EN has an internal pull-up, so while
#   the MCU pin is high-Z (reset, bootloader) the BEC runs and the VTX keeps
#   video.  OUTPUT HIGH here; RELAY2 must default ON (defaults.parm) because
#   AP_Relay::init() otherwise drives the pin to RELAY2_DEFAULT = 0 (off).
# VTX_12V_SEL (PD11) -> R37 1k -> Q1 2N7002 gate, R38 100k gate pull-down.
#   Q1 parallels R36 26.7k with R35 10k (bottom FB): OFF = 8.96 V, ON = 12.02 V.
#   High-Z / LOW = 9 V, so 12 V can only exist while firmware drives it HIGH.
#   12 V is a 4S-only mode (regulation needs Vin >= ~13.3 V at 2 A); see
#   firmware/vtx_power and ardupilot/scripts/vtx_bec.lua for the interlock.
# VTX_VSENSE (PC5 = ADC12_INP8) <- R40 10k / R41 1k divider of +VTX (x11.0).
#   Exposed as battery monitor 2 (voltage only): BATT2_VOLT_PIN 8,
#   BATT2_VOLT_MULT 11.0 (defaults.parm).  Shares the ADC1 DMA stream.
# PD10/PD11 sit next to PD12 (32.768 kHz IMU_CLKIN_MON) - route them away.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PD10 VTX_PWR     OUTPUT PUSHPULL SPEED_LOW HIGH GPIO(81)
PD11 VTX_12V_SEL OUTPUT PUSHPULL SPEED_LOW LOW  GPIO(82)
define RELAY2_PIN_DEFAULT 81
define RELAY3_PIN_DEFAULT 82
PC5  VTX_VSENSE  ADC1 SCALE(1)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OSD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
define OSD_ENABLED 1
define HAL_OSD_TYPE_DEFAULT 1
ROMFS_WILDCARD libraries/AP_OSD/fonts/font*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DMA STREAM BUDGET (STM32H743: DMA1 + DMA2 = 16 streams via DMAMUX1)
#
# Resolved by dma_resolver.py and verified against the generated hwdef.h
# (python3 tools/validate_dma.py):
#
#  stream  request(s)               consumer                     policy
#  DMA1-0  TIM1_UP (+CH1,CH3 *)     DShot out + eRPM capture     NOSHARE
#                                   (all 4 motors, round-robin)
#  DMA1-1  SPI1_RX                  IMU1 ICM-42688-P             NOSHARE
#  DMA1-2  SPI1_TX                  IMU1 ICM-42688-P             NOSHARE
#  DMA1-3  SPI4_RX                  IMU2 ICM-42688-P             NOSHARE
#  DMA1-4  SPI4_TX                  IMU2 ICM-42688-P             NOSHARE
#  DMA1-5  USART1_RX                DisplayPort / MAVLink        NOSHARE
#  DMA1-6  USART1_TX                DisplayPort / MAVLink        NOSHARE
#  DMA1-7  ADC1                     battery V/I
#  DMA2-0  USART2_RX                CRSF / ELRS
#  DMA2-1  USART3_RX                GPS
#  (UART7_RX, Rev 13.0: NODMA - VTX connector SBUS / DJI HDL)
#  DMA2-2  SPI2_TX                  OSD                          shareable
#  DMA2-5  SPI2_RX                  OSD                          shareable
#  free    DMA2-3, DMA2-4, DMA2-6, DMA2-7  (4 spare streams)
#
#  * On DMAMUX parts ArduPilot deliberately multiplexes TIMx_CHy input
#    capture onto the TIMx_UP stream: bidir DShot is half-duplex in time
#    (frame out on UP, DMAMUX re-pointed to CHy for the eRPM reply), so the
#    whole motor group costs ONE stream. This is not inter-peripheral
#    sharing - SHARED_DMA_MASK in hwdef.h is 0.
#
#  Not on any stream:
#    SDMMC1    internal IDMA master
#    I2C1      DMA excluded on H7 by chibios_hwdef.py
#    FDCAN1    dedicated message RAM
#    OTG1      USB OTG_FS internal FIFO
#    USART2_TX, USART3_TX, UART7_RX   NODMA (interrupt driven, low volume)
#
# DMA_NOSHARE pins the latency-critical set (IMUs, motors, USART1) so the
# resolver can never share them even if future peripherals exhaust the
# budget. DMA_PRIORITY only sets dma_resolver.py's allocation/sharing order
# (highest first); it does NOT set hardware arbitration priority. Hardware
# stream priority is fixed by ArduPilot (not overridable from hwdef):
#   TIM1 DShot/eRPM  PL3 very-high (RCOutput.cpp / RCOutput_bdshot.cpp)
#   SDMMC1           3  (IDMA, separate AXI master - no stream arbitration)
#   ADC1             2  (stm32h7_mcuconf.h STM32_ADC_ADC12_DMA_PRIORITY)
#   SPI1/SPI2/SPI4   1  (STM32_SPI_SPIn_DMA_PRIORITY)
#   USARTn           0  (STM32_UART_USARTn_DMA_PRIORITY)
# Validate with: python3 tools/validate_dma.py --ardupilot <tree>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DMA_PRIORITY TIM1* SPI1* SPI4* USART1* ADC1* USART2* USART3* SPI2*
DMA_NOSHARE  TIM1* SPI1* SPI4* USART1*

# build ABIN for flash-from-bootloader support
env BUILD_ABIN True
